  <div class="col-lg-8">
        <img class="blog-hero-image" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="5th class result rajasthan board">
        <div class="blog-content">
            <div class="blog-body">
                <h1 class="blog-title text-center mb-4">RBSE 5th Class Result 2026: Your Gateway to the Next Academic Chapter is HERE!</h1>

                <p>The much-awaited results for the Rajasthan Board 5th Class examinations have officially been declared, bringing an end to the anticipation for lakhs of students across the state. On March 24, 2026, the Rajasthan Board of Secondary Education (RBSE) released the Class 5 results, alongside the Class 8 and Class 10 results, marking a significant moment for young learners and their families. This year's results showcase a commendable performance by students, paving the way for their academic progression.</p>

                <div class="highlight-text">
                    "The Rajasthan Board has declared the Class 5 results with an impressive overall pass percentage of 97.75%. Congratulations to all the successful students!"
                </div>

                <h2 class="section-title">How to Check Your RBSE 5th Class Result 2026</h2>
                <p>Accessing your Rajasthan Board 5th Class result is a straightforward process. Students and parents can check the provisional scorecards online through various official portals. Here’s a step-by-step guide to help you retrieve the results quickly:</p>

                <div class="benefit-item">
                  <div class="benefit-title">1. Visit the Official Websites</div>
                  <div class="benefit-content">Head to any of the designated official Rajasthan Board portals. The primary websites for checking results are: rajshaladarpan.nic.in, rajeduboard.rajasthan.gov.in, rajresults.nic.in, and rajpsp.nic.in.</div>
                </div>

                <div class="benefit-item">
                  <div class="benefit-title">2. Locate the Result Link</div>
                  <div class="benefit-content">On the homepage, look for the link specifically for "RBSE Class 5 Result 2026" or "Rajasthan Class 5 Result 2026."</div>
                </div>

                <div class="benefit-item">
                  <div class="benefit-title">3. Enter Your Credentials</div>
                  <div class="benefit-content">You will be redirected to a login page where you need to enter your roll number and date of birth. Some portals might also require your district, application number, or school NIC-SD code/PSP code.</div>
                </div>

                <div class="benefit-item">
                  <div class="benefit-title">4. Complete the Captcha</div>
                  <div class="benefit-content">Enter the displayed captcha code for verification purposes.</div>
                </div>

                <div class="benefit-item">
                  <div class="benefit-title">5. View and Download Your Marksheet</div>
                  <div class="benefit-content">After submitting the details, your RBSE 5th Class result will appear on the screen. It is advisable to download and print the provisional marksheet for future reference.</div>
                </div>

                <h2 class="section-title">Key Statistics and Performance Highlights</h2>
                <p>This year's 5th Class results reflect a strong academic year for students in Rajasthan. Here are some of the key highlights:</p>

                <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                  <p>✅ Overall Pass Percentage: 97.75%</p>
                  <p>✅ Total Students Passed: 13,33,936 out of 13,68,947 appeared</p>
                  <p>✅ Girls Outperform Boys: Girls achieved a pass percentage of 97.94%, while boys stood at 97.59%. This indicates a gender gap of 0.35% in favor of girls.</p>
                </div>

                <p>The consistently high success rate at the elementary level underscores the effectiveness of learning outcomes and assessment systems within Rajasthan's education framework.</p>

                <h2 class="section-title">Understanding the Grading System and Passing Criteria</h2>
                <p>A significant change has been implemented this year, as the previous policy of automatic promotion for all Class 5 students has been abolished. To pass the RBSE Class 5 examinations, students are now required to secure a minimum of 33% marks in each subject. The board awards subject-wise grades rather than aggregate marks, using a five-point scale from A to E.</p>

                <table>
                  <thead>
                    <tr>
                      <th>Grade</th>
                      <th>Marks Range</th>
                      <th>Interpretation</th>
                    </tr>
                  </thead>
                  <tbody>
                    <tr>
                      <td>A1</td>
                      <td>91 to 100%</td>
                      <td>Excellent Performance</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>A2</td>
                      <td>81 to 90%</td>
                      <td>Very Good Performance</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>B1</td>
                      <td>71 to 80%</td>
                      <td>Good Performance</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>B2</td>
                      <td>61 to 70%</td>
                      <td>Above Average Performance</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>C1</td>
                      <td>51 to 60%</td>
                      <td>Average Performance</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>C2</td>
                      <td>41 to 50%</td>
                      <td>Fair Performance</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>D</td>
                      <td>33 to 40%</td>
                      <td>Satisfactory Performance (Pass)</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>E</td>
                      <td>Below 33%</td>
                      <td>Needs Improvement (Supplementary Category)</td>
                    </tr>
                  </tbody>
                </table>
                <p>A grade of 'D' or above in each subject is considered a passing grade. The online result serves as a provisional scorecard, and students must collect their original marksheets and certificates from their respective schools after the official declaration.</p>

                <h2 class="section-title">Supplementary Examinations: A Second Chance</h2>
                <p>For students who, unfortunately, do not achieve the minimum passing marks (Grade E) in one or more subjects, the Rajasthan Board provides a crucial opportunity to improve their performance. A total of 30,640 Class 5 students have been placed in the supplementary category this year. These students will be eligible to appear for re-examinations, which are expected to be conducted in July 2026. This initiative aims to help students save their academic year and continue their educational journey without significant delays.</p>

                <h2 class="section-title">Looking Ahead</h2>
                <p>The successful declaration of the 5th Class results is a testament to the hard work of students, dedication of teachers, and efforts of the Rajasthan Board. As students transition to higher classes, they are encouraged to continue building a strong educational foundation. For those preparing for supplementary exams, diligent preparation can lead to success in the upcoming re-assessment.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
  </div>

            
            
